      "content": "<p><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@sajal24x7\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">@sajal24x7</a> 1) I don't think people type domains so the length is not really a factor 2) for \"smart\" plays with short names... be worry of jurisdictions. Both `.tt`, `.rs`, `.al` and others are COUNTRY TLDs. Which means you are bound by these countries laws. See for example past risk on `bit.ly`, under Lybian rules. Make sure to read all fine prints in contracts, do not blindly click \"Accept\" and become bound by Albanian (.al) laws on domains without knowing…</p>",
      "url": "https://framapiaf.org/@pmevzek/116930882392848033",
      "published": "2026-07-16T17:41:09.000Z",
      "status": "approved"
    },
    {
      "id": "mastodon:reply:116934583454615759",
      "type": "reply",
      "platform": "mastodon",
      "author": {
        "name": "Sajal Choudhary",
